{"book":11,"chapter":11,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / THE JAVASCRIPT LANGUAGE / CHAPTER 11","slides":[{"title":"FP in JavaScript","sub":"Chapter 11 · The main way to write reliable code","short":"Introduction","main":"Functions are values; libraries grew around them.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Functions are values","Libraries","Ideas in Redux and React"],"captions":["In JavaScript functional style is not exotic: functions are values, with closures, map, filter and reduce","Libraries grew around it: Ramda, lodash/fp, Immer, RxJS","Redux and React rest on the same ideas: pure functions, immutability, composition"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["const total = items","  .map(price)","  .filter(isValid)","  .reduce(sum, 0);"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"js","size":11.5,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"l0","x":66.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Ramda","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l1","x":196.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"lodash/fp","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l2","x":66.0,"y":102.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Immer","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l3","x":196.0,"y":102.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"RxJS","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Redux","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"React","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":170.0,"y":116.0,"w":200.0,"h":28.0,"text":"pure functions · immutability","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.1,29.1]}]},{"title":"Pure function","sub":"Referential transparency","short":"Purity","main":"Same result for same arguments, no changes outside.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Definition","Impure","Benefits"],"captions":["A pure function gives one result for the same arguments and changes nothing outside: referential transparency","Impure: Math.random, Date.now, mutating an argument, console.log, touching the DOM, reading a file","Pure functions are tested without mocks and are safe to cache, reorder and run in parallel"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const add = (a, b) => a + b;","","add(2, 3)   // always 5","// can be replaced with 5"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["const f1 = () => Math.random();","const f2 = () => Date.now();","const f3 = (a) => a.push(1);","const f4 = (x) => console.log(x);"],"bad":[0,1,2,3],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p0","x":66.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"tests without mocks","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p1","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"caching","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p2","x":294.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"parallelism","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.0,31.1]}]},{"title":"Effects at the edges","sub":"Core and shell","short":"Effects","main":"Pass time and randomness as parameters.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Core and shell","Dependency injection","Testing"],"captions":["Effects are needed but kept apart from computation: pure core inside, I/O at the edges","Pass the current time or a random number as a parameter, so a test can supply a fixed one","Logic is tested instantly; the thin layer touching the world is tested separately"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":240.0,"h":100.0,"text":"","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"text":"shell: I/O","tone":"muted","size":9.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":84.0,"w":130.0,"h":50.0,"text":"pure core","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const makeId = (rand) =>","  'id' + Math.floor(rand() * 1000);","","makeId(() => 0.5)   // 'id500'"],"hl":[3],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"core: test","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"shell: mock","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"many fast tests + few integration tests","size":9.5}]],"cues":[12.1,27.3]}]},{"title":"Immutability","sub":"New instead of editing","short":"Immutability","main":"const is not immutability; structural sharing makes it cheap.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["const ≠ immutable","Non-mutating methods","Structural sharing"],"captions":["const only forbids rebinding; real immutability means creating a new value instead of editing","Safe: map, filter, slice, toSorted, toSpliced, with; dangerous: push, pop, splice, reverse, sort mutate in place","Updating a nested object copies only the nodes on the path from the root; the rest is shared with the old version"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["const a = [1, 2, 3];","a.push(4);          // allowed!","const b = [...a, 5];  // new"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"g","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"map · filter · slice","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"g2","x":90.0,"y":90.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"toSorted · with","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"push · pop · splice","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r2","x":270.0,"y":90.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"sort · reverse","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"left: new, right: in place","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":70.0,"h":24.0,"text":"state","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":270.0,"y":40.0,"w":70.0,"h":24.0,"text":"state'","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"u","x":70.0,"y":90.0,"w":60.0,"h":22.0,"text":"user","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"u2","x":250.0,"y":90.0,"w":60.0,"h":22.0,"text":"user'","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"i","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"w":60.0,"h":22.0,"text":"items","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":90.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":70.0,"y2":80.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":270.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":250.0,"y2":80.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":90.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":160.0,"y2":120.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e4","x1":270.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":200.0,"y2":120.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[25.7,45.5]}]},{"title":"Higher-order functions","sub":"map, filter, reduce","short":"map, reduce","main":"Describe the data transformation, not the traversal.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["map, filter, reduce","reduce is universal","Declarative"],"captions":["map transforms, filter selects, reduce folds a collection into one value; flatMap, some, every, find nearby","map, filter, grouping, counting and unique values can all be expressed with reduce","Instead of a loop with mutable counters, a chain of steps: each can be read, tested and replaced separately"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"f0","x":66.0,"y":60.0,"w":96.0,"h":34.0,"text":"map","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f1","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":96.0,"h":34.0,"text":"filter","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f2","x":294.0,"y":60.0,"w":96.0,"h":34.0,"text":"reduce","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":114.0,"text":"also: flatMap · some · every · find","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const countBy = (xs, f) =>","  xs.reduce((acc, x) => {","    const k = f(x);","    return { ...acc, [k]: (acc[k] ?? 0) + 1 };","  }, {});"],"hl":[3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let t = 0;","for (let i = 0; i < xs.length; i++) {","  if (xs[i] > 0) t += xs[i] * 2;","}","// ↔  xs.filter(gt0).map(dbl).reduce(add)"],"hl":[4],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[11.6,27.2]}]},{"title":"Composition","sub":"compose, pipe, tap","short":"Composition","main":"pipe reads left to right.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["compose","pipe","tap"],"captions":["Composing two functions applies the second first, then the first, as in math","pipe does the same left to right, as we read text: data flows from step to step","To debug, insert tap between steps: it prints the value and returns it unchanged"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["const compose = (f, g) => (x) => f(g(x));","","compose(inc, dbl)(5)   // inc(dbl(5)) = 11"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const pipe = (...fs) => (x) =>","  fs.reduce((acc, f) => f(acc), x);","","pipe(trim, upper, exclaim)('hello')"],"hl":[3],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const tap = (f) => (x) => (f(x), x);","","pipe(parse, tap(console.log), double)"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[14.7,29.5]}]},{"title":"Currying","sub":"Partial application","short":"Currying","main":"Data goes last.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Currying","Partial application","Data goes last"],"captions":["Currying turns a function of several arguments into a chain of one-argument functions","Partial application fixes some arguments and returns a function for the rest","If data is the last argument, a partially applied function fits straight into a chain as a step"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["const add = (a) => (b) => a + b;","","add(2)(3)   // 5"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const mul = (k) => (x) => k * x;","const triple = mul(3);","triple(7)   // 21"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const map = (f) => (xs) => xs.map(f);","","pipe(filter(isOdd), map(mul(3)))([1, 2, 3])"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.1,33.1]}]},{"title":"Recursion","sub":"Stack limit and trampoline","short":"Recursion","main":"A trampoline does not grow the stack.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Recursion instead of a loop","Stack limit","Trampoline"],"captions":["Recursion suits tree walks, subset search and parsing nested structures","Most engines have no tail call optimization: thousands of steps fail with RangeError","Trampoline: the function returns a step function and an outer loop calls the steps one by one, keeping the stack flat"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const sum = ([h, ...t]) =>","  h === undefined ? 0 : h + sum(t);","","sum([1, 2, 3])   // 6"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":130.0,"y":140.0,"w":120.0,"h":20.0,"text":"sum(…0)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":130.0,"y":116.0,"w":120.0,"h":20.0,"text":"sum(…1)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":130.0,"y":92.0,"w":120.0,"h":20.0,"text":"sum(…2)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s3","x":130.0,"y":68.0,"w":120.0,"h":20.0,"text":"sum(…3)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s4","x":130.0,"y":44.0,"w":120.0,"h":20.0,"text":"sum(…4)","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":280.0,"y":76.0,"text":"RangeError:\nmax call stack","tone":"red","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":26.0,"lines":["const trampoline = (f) => (...a) => {","  let r = f(...a);","  while (typeof r === 'function') r = r();","  return r;","};"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":19.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[19.6,29.2]}]},{"title":"Maybe and Either","sub":"Sum types","short":"Maybe, Either","main":"Explicit data instead of null and exceptions.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Tags","Maybe","Either"],"captions":["Sum types in JavaScript are objects with a tag field; switch on the tag works like pattern matching","Maybe: «has a value» or «nothing»; replaces null with explicit data and forces handling both cases","Either: «success with a value» or «failure with a reason»; replaces exceptions; ?. is a tiny built-in Maybe"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const area = (s) => {","  switch (s.type) {","    case 'circle': return PI * s.r ** 2;","    case 'rect':   return s.w * s.h;","  }","};"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":19.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"j","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Just(5)","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":250.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Nothing","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"map skips Nothing","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Right(5)","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":250.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Left(error)","tone":"red","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"map skips Left","size":10.0}]],"cues":[13.5,30.6]}]},{"title":"Functors and monads","sub":"map and flatMap","short":"Functors","main":"A «might fail» chain is written flat.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Functor","Laws","Monad"],"captions":["A container with map is a functor: Array, Maybe, Either; map works inside and keeps the shape","Law 1: map(x => x) changes nothing. Law 2: map(f ∘ g) equals map(g) then map(f)","With flatMap too (apply a function returning a container and flatten) it is a monad: flatMap for arrays, then for promises"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"[1, 2, 3]","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":140.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":222.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"text":"map(f)","size":10.0,"mono":true},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"[f(1), f(2), f(3)]","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["xs.map(x => x)   ≡  xs","","xs.map(x => f(g(x)))","  ≡  xs.map(g).map(f)"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["[1, 2].flatMap(x => [x, x * 10])","// [1, 10, 2, 20]","","fetchUser(1).then(u => fetchPosts(u.id))"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[15.0,35.4]}]},{"title":"Laziness","sub":"Generators and iterators","short":"Laziness","main":"A lazy pipeline creates no intermediate arrays.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Generators","No intermediate arrays","Iterator helpers"],"captions":["Generators yield values one by one: from an infinite sequence you can take the first ten","A lazy pipeline creates no intermediate arrays: each element goes through all the steps in full","New iterator methods map, filter, take give lazy chains without libraries; but laziness makes debugging harder"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["function* nat() {","  let n = 1;","  while (true) yield n++;","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"e0","x":60.0,"y":50.0,"w":30.0,"h":22.0,"text":"1","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e1","x":80.0,"y":80.0,"w":30.0,"h":22.0,"text":"2","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e2","x":100.0,"y":110.0,"w":30.0,"h":22.0,"text":"3","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":230.0,"y":76.0,"text":"map → filter → take\nelement by element","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["nat()","  .map((x) => x * x)","  .filter((x) => x % 2)","  .take(4)","  .toArray();   // [1, 9, 25, 49]"],"hl":[4],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[13.7,27.4]}]},{"title":"Application architecture","sub":"Reducer and selectors","short":"Reducer","main":"State is a fold of actions.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Reducer","Fold of actions","Selectors"],"captions":["State is one object; a reducer is a pure function of old state and action that returns the new one","State at any moment is the fold of all actions since the start: history can be replayed, rolled back and recorded","Selectors are pure functions from state to what to show; they can be memoized; effects live apart"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["const reducer = (s, a) => {","  switch (a.type) {","    case 'add': return [...s, a.item];","    case 'del': return s.filter(x => x.id !== a.id);","    default: return s;","  }","};"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":18.0,"w":335.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["const state = actions.reduce(reducer, []);","","// undo = actions.slice(0, -1).reduce(…)"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":80.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"state","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":126.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":164.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"sel","x":200.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":34.0,"text":"selector","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":236.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":274.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"v","x":320.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":34.0,"text":"view","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.7,28.6]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: ready-made FP libraries.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Purity","Transformations","Next"],"captions":["A pure function depends only on its arguments, effects go to the edges; immutability means new values instead of edits","map, filter, reduce, composition, currying, trampoline, Maybe and Either, lazy iterators; state is a fold of actions","Next: ready-made libraries: Ramda, lodash/fp, Immer, RxJS, lenses"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"pure functions","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":240.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"immutability","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":160.0,"y":116.0,"w":190.0,"h":28.0,"text":"effects at the edges","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"pipe · curry","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":240.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Maybe · Either","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":160.0,"y":116.0,"w":190.0,"h":28.0,"text":"reduce(reducer, init)","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":30.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["import * as R from 'ramda';","R.pipe(R.map(R.inc), R.sum)([1, 2])"],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"chapter 12: FP libraries and techniques","size":9.5}]],"cues":[16.3,27.1]}]}]}